#   because refs/pull/* are hidden and GitHub rejects creating them in a normal repo.
# - The source contains large APK binaries (GitHub warned about files above 50 MB).
#
# Requested feature to port next:
# - https://github.com/komikku-app/anikku/pull/264
# - Title: feat: Add Airing Schedule tab + navigation reorder (Updates → More, History
#   2nd, Schedule 3rd)
# - Status at research time: OPEN, not merged
# - Base: 7ebdc04d97ea40bc5aec4c27d23caaa14870c247
# - Head: f0d608d090ddda4f8fc0fb50dbf7985d8fb111fc
# - Head branch: shan-test-project/anikku:feat/airing-schedule
# - The PR is 25 files, approximately 2,720 additions and 11 deletions.
#
# PR implementation map:
# 1. mihon.feature.airingschedule.AiringScheduleRepository
#    - Calls https://graphql.anilist.co/ with a weekly AiringSchedule GraphQL query.
#    - Fetches Monday 00:00 through the following Monday minus one second, 50 rows per
#      page, up to 10 pages. It retries 429/502/503/504 and IO failures up to 5 times
#      with exponential backoff, jitter, and a 500 ms delay between pages.
#    - Maps AniList schedule/media/title/cover/episode/status/score/format/adult/genre
#      fields into AiringScheduleEntry. Adult entries are filtered before display.
# 2. AiringScheduleEntry
#    - Stable scheduleId/mediaId/episode/airingAt model with English, Romaji, native,
#      and user-preferred title fallbacks; hasAired() compares epoch seconds.
# 3. AiringScheduleScreenModel + AiringScheduleTab + ScheduleAnimeCard
#    - Loads the current week, groups entries by local day, and displays a day pager.
#    - Observes the anime library and source preferences. Source matching is title-based
#      across normalized title candidates; keep this limitation in mind for aliases.
#    - Supports title language, adult visibility, favorite/pinned-source filtering,
#      auto-add from pinned sources, source upload-delay adjustment, search/add-to-library,
#      and notification bell actions.
# 4. SchedulePreferences + SettingsScheduleScreen
#    - Stores favorite source IDs, filters, title language, adult toggle, manual/custom
#      delay, learned source delays, auto-refresh settings, and notification IDs/alarm keys.
#    - Auto-refresh choices are 1–7 days (default 7). Upload-delay choices are 30 min,
#      1/2/6/12 hours, custom, or never. Settings start/cancel the workers reactively.
# 5. ScheduleDataRefreshWorker
#    - Unique WorkManager periodic job, network-constrained, caches the current week in
#      schedule_cache.json, retries transient failures, and re-arms series alarms after
#      each refresh. It is disabled unless the user enables auto-refresh.
# 6. ScheduleRefreshWorker + UploadDelayTracker
#    - Periodically compares AniList air times with matching library anime episode upload
#      times to learn per-source delay. It caps source calls per run at 12 and smooths each
#      observation with 60% previous value / 40% new value. Custom and Never cancel it.
# 7. ScheduleNotifications + ScheduleAlarmReceiver
#    - Uses mediaId:episode alarm keys, AlarmManager exact alarms, and a receiver that
#      posts a high-priority notification with cover image and a search action in MainActivity.
#    - Android 12+ exact-alarm permission is checked/requested. Persisted alarm-key writes
#      are serialized with a mutex because UI, workers, and receivers can race.
# 8. Navigation/settings/resources
#    - Adds AiringScheduleTab and changes NavStyle to include it between History and Browse;
#      MOVE_SCHEDULE_TO_MORE can move it into More. Adds schedule settings and translated
#      strings, notification channel/ID, DI bindings, receiver manifest entry, and a small
#      CloudflareInterceptor change.
#
# AniZen adaptation cautions:
# - AniZen is an anime fork, and this PR is already anime-oriented (GetLibraryAnime,
#   ScheduleAnimeCard, anime episode_number/source APIs), so the domain model direction is
#   compatible. Still verify package names and current AniZen APIs before applying files.
# - Do not blindly apply the PR's AndroidManifest deletions. Preserve AniZen's existing
#   anizen OAuth deep-link scheme, tracker hosts, Google OAuth scheme, updater receiver,
#   and existing service attributes; add only the schedule receiver/permissions needed.
# - Check AniZen's icon/resources before using the PR's ic_komikku notification icon.
# - Merge only the schedule strings into AniZen's current i18n/resource files. The PR's
#   base-string edits are not a substitute for regenerating AniZen's Moko resources.
# - Review the CloudflareInterceptor hunk independently; it is not inherently required
#   by the schedule UI and should not weaken existing network behavior.
# - The PR's default NavStyle changes existing navigation behavior. Decide explicitly
#   whether AniZen should use Schedule as a primary tab or place it under More.
# - AniList is public but rate-limited; retain the retry/page-delay behavior and test with
#   both empty schedules and HTTP 429 responses. No API key belongs in the app.
#
# Recommended port order:
# 1. Add the model/repository and verify GraphQL parsing with the existing NetworkHelper/Json.
# 2. Add preferences, DI, cache worker, and screen model; validate date/time-zone boundaries.
# 3. Add the tab/card UI and navigation without changing unrelated manifest/deep-link behavior.
# 4. Add upload-delay learning and settings after the basic schedule renders reliably.
# 5. Add alarms/notifications and Android exact-alarm handling last, then test reboot,
#    duplicate toggles, already-aired episodes, and series rescheduling.
# 6. Run Spotless, compile the preview APK, and manually test tracker logins, custom covers,
#    Feed/Recommendations, schedule refresh, and notification permission flows together.
#
# Current state: research only; schedule code has not been applied to AniZen_modified.
